{"timestamp":1774892952423,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"b1685d0e-5b94-40d6-819c-468743fc3bcf","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_016Htxj3GjPQea3rXY8TSsTy","payload":{"session_id":"b1685d0e-5b94-40d6-819c-468743fc3bcf","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-c39aac7b/b1685d0e-5b94-40d6-819c-468743fc3bcf.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c39aac7b","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c39aac7b/specs/patch/patch-copyFragment-integration-test.md","content":"# Patch: Add copyFragment \u2192 generateUniqueFragmentTitle integration test\n\n## Metadata\nadw_id: ``\nreview_change_request: `Issue #1: No integration test covers the copyFragment \u2192 generateUniqueFragmentTitle call path. The helper is tested in isolation but nothing asserts that copyFragment passes the correct (requestedTitle, parentPath) arguments. Resolution: Add a test in the copyFragment describe block that stubs generateUniqueFragmentTitle and asserts it is called with the expected arguments derived from result.path and updatedTitle. Severity: tech_debt`\n\n## Issue Summary\n**Original Spec:** n/a\n**Issue:** `copyFragment` was changed to derive `requestedTitle` from `updatedTitle`/`result.title` and `parentPath` from `result.path`, then delegate to `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`. There is no test that stubs `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` on the repository instance and asserts that `copyFragment` calls it with the exact `(requestedTitle, parentPath)` arguments.\n**Solution:** Add a `describe('copyFragment', ...)` block in `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` with a single test. The test stubs `aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy` to return a controlled fragment, stubs `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to reject (halting execution before the untestable `#addToCache`), calls `copyFragment('Updated Title')`, and asserts the stub was called with `('Updated Title', parentPath)` where `parentPath` is derived by dropping the last segment of `result.path`.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` \u2014 add `describe('copyFragment', ...)` block before `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', ...)`\n\n## Implementation Steps\n\n### Step 1: Insert the new describe block\nInsert the following block at line 1526 (between the closing `});` of `describe('deleteFragment', ...)` and the opening of `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', ...)`):\n\n```js\n    describe('copyFragment', () => {\n        it('calls generateUniqueFragmentTitle with requestedTitle derived from updatedTitle and parentPath derived from result.path', async () => {\n            const repository = createRepository();\n            const copiedFragment = {\n                id: 'copied-id',\n                path: '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards/cloned-card',\n                title: 'Original Title',\n                fields: [{ name: 'osi', values: [] }],\n            };\n\n            repository.fragmentInEdit = { id: 'source-id' };\n            repository.operation = { set: sandbox.stub() };\n            repository.search = { value: { path: undefined } };\n            repository.processError = sandbox.stub();\n\n            repository.aem = {\n                sites: { cf: { fragments: { copy: sandbox.stub().resolves(copiedFragment) } } },\n            };\n\n            const generateStub = sandbox\n                .stub(repository, 'generateUniqueFragmentTitle')\n                .rejects(new Error('stop'));\n\n            await repository.copyFragment('Updated Title');\n\n            const expectedParentPath = '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards';\n            expect(generateStub.calledOnce).to.be.true;\n            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[0]).to.equal('Updated Title');\n            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[1]).to.equal(expectedParentPath);\n        });\n\n        it('passes result.title as requestedTitle when updatedTitle equals result.title', async () => {\n            const repository = createRepository();\n            const copiedFragment = {\n                id: 'copied-id',\n                path: '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards/cloned-card',\n                title: 'Same Title',\n                fields: [],\n            };\n\n            repository.fragmentInEdit = { id: 'source-id' };\n            repository.operation = { set: sandbox.stub() };\n            repository.search = { value: { path: undefined } };\n            repository.processError = sandbox.stub();\n\n            repository.aem = {\n                sites: { cf: { fragments: { copy: sandbox.stub().resolves(copiedFragment) } } },\n            };\n\n            const generateStub = sandbox\n                .stub(repository, 'generateUniqueFragmentTitle')\n                .rejects(new Error('stop'));\n\n            await repository.copyFragment('Same Title');\n\n            expect(generateStub.calledOnce).to.be.true;\n            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[0]).to.equal('Same Title');\n            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[1]).to.equal('/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards');\n        });\n    });\n```\n\n- Place between line 1525 (`});` closing `deleteFragment`) and line 1527 (`describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle'`)\n- No new imports needed \u2014 `sandbox`, `createRepository`, `createFragment` are already in scope\n\n### Step 2: Verify syntax\nRun `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` to confirm no parse errors.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nnode --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js\n```\n\n```bash\ncd studio && npx web-test-runner test/mas-repository.test.js --node-resolve --coverage 2>&1 | grep -E \"copyFragment|passed|failed|error\"\n```\n\n## Patch Scope\n**Lines of code to change:** ~45 (insert only, no deletions)\n**Risk level:** low\n**Testing required:** Run `mas-repository.test.js` and confirm the two new `copyFragment` tests pass alongside all existing tests\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Htxj3GjPQea3rXY8TSsTy"}}
